index 0000000..5d2a349
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/attempt-manager-async-context-manager-248b14e6b437457d.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+---
+features:
+  - |
+    The attempt object yielded by ``AsyncRetrying`` now supports the async
+    context-manager protocol, so ``async with attempt:`` works inside an
+    ``async for attempt in AsyncRetrying(...)`` loop. It behaves exactly like
+    ``with attempt:``: exceptions are recorded as the attempt's outcome and
+    retried, ``reraise=True`` re-raises the last exception, and
+    ``attempt.retry_state.set_result(...)`` still works. Previously it raised
+    ``TypeError``.
